  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "trampoline--intro-css-fd8ce4f3-ba8e-4404-b5b4-f5d945b945f0",
        "text": "So far, our owl webpage has all the facts and content thanks to HTML. But it looks a bit plain, doesn't it?",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/637be65871beb50d290fb8a18074ae6d-trampoline--intro-css-panel-1-4ec1106a-12a8-4463-b180-e732d48486a1.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "trampoline--intro-css-eb3e7f7a-eb8b-46be-b2ec-1ac555c6e36c",
        "text": "CSS is like our webpage's personal stylist! It gives us the power to add vibrant colors, choose cool fonts, and arrange everything beautifully on the page.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/834100a1b1212d81ed3f88f168497703-trampoline--intro-css-panel-2-c6fb1a7b-a22e-470a-9f5a-d81724c9bcef.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "trampoline--intro-css-29754032-1852-4522-8390-e9bd2055ae94",
        "text": "Together, HTML builds the strong foundation and content, while CSS paints the beautiful picture. This combination creates an engaging and informative experience, just like a digital poster about owls!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/4e981704ad6970fbb3167b8c071fe14d-trampoline--intro-css-panel-3-b25428cc-565e-4711-a17c-1a68eed6925a.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Introduce CSS as the language for styling webpages. Explain how CSS works with HTML to change colors, fonts, and layout. Show a visual comparison of an unstyled versus styled page."
  },
